THOUGHT: info.data is declared @Nullable, and although loadAsync enforces non-null with an exception, NullAway doesn’t connect that guarantee to loadSync. I should add an explicit local non-null variable in loadSync, using a null-check (and throwing if violated) before passing it to Texture.load / new Texture. Then I’ll run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '90,98s/^/@@@/;90,98p' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/assets/loaders/TextureLoader.java && sed -i '90,101c\  @Nullable
  @Override
  public Texture loadSync(
      AssetManager manager,
      String fileName,
      FileHandle file,
      @Nullable TextureParameter parameter) {
    if (info == null) return null;
    TextureData data = info.data;
    if (data == null)
      throw new IllegalStateException("TextureData must not be null in loadSync");
    Texture texture = info.texture;
    if (texture != null) {
      texture.load(data);
    } else {
      texture = new Texture(data);
    }
    if (parameter != null) {
      texture.setFilter(parameter.minFilter, parameter.magFilter);
      texture.setWrap(parameter.wrapU, parameter.wrapV);
    }
    return texture;
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/assets/loaders/TextureLoader.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway|error: \[NULL_DEREFERENCE|PASS_NULLABLE" -n new_build_output.log | head```

